1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This is Unpause—a way back into
the things you love making.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
When you finally have ten spare minutes,

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
remembering where you stopped
can use most of them.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Unpause keeps your next small step ready.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
After a little making,
leave yourself a handoff:

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
what changed, what to do next,
how long it might take,

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
and where you put the pieces.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Your next session starts with context.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,500
Add a photo if it helps,
then save your place.

10
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:40,000
The record stays on your device.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Each return becomes a checkpoint.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You can see the small steps adding up,
without a streak to protect

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
or a deadline to miss.

14
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Your work is still here when you are.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Choose the time and energy
you have today,

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
and find something that fits.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Across sewing, woodwork, art,
or your own kind of making,

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
this is one home
for your half-made things.

19
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
I’m Shivam Gupta, creator of Unpause.

20
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,990
Less remembering. More making.
